---
layout: article
title: Mention the reviewer
description: Mention Appwrite Reviews in a pull request comment to request a new review, ask about a change, or teach it a preference, on GitHub, GitLab, Gitea, Bitbucket, and Origin.
---

Mention the reviewer in a comment on a pull request to talk to it. What it does depends on what you ask.

# Request a review {% #request-a-review %}

`@appwrite review` reviews the whole pull request again, at its latest commit. Use it for a pull request that was open before you turned on reviews, or in a repository where automatic reviews are off.

A review you request costs [credits](/docs/products/reviews/billing) like any other review.

# Ask a question {% #ask-a-question %}

Any other mention gets one answer in the thread:

```text
@appwrite could this query run without an index?
```

The reviewer reads the code to answer, but doesn't change it. Answers are free.

To discuss a finding, reply in its thread. You don't need to mention the reviewer there.

# Teach a preference {% #teach-a-preference %}

Ask the reviewer to remember how your team works:

```text
@appwrite remember that we use early returns instead of nested conditions
```

The preference becomes a [learning](/docs/products/reviews/learnings), and later reviews and answers in the repository follow it.

# Who the reviewer answers {% #who-the-reviewer-answers %}

The reviewer only acts on comments from people with access to the repository, such as its owners, members, and collaborators. On Origin, that means people with write or admin permission on the repository. Mentions inside code blocks and quoted lines are ignored.

# Mentions by provider {% #providers %}

How you mention the reviewer depends on your Git provider:

| Provider | Mention |
|----------|---------|
| GitHub | `@appwrite`, the Appwrite GitHub App |
| GitLab | The account that connected GitLab to Appwrite. Reviews are posted as that account |
| Gitea | The account that connected Gitea to Appwrite. Reviews are posted as that account |
| Bitbucket | `@appwrite`, typed as plain text. Reviews are posted as the account that connected Bitbucket |
| Origin | `@appwrite`, typed as plain text. The Appwrite app posts the reviews |

On GitLab, Gitea, and Bitbucket, connect with a dedicated account if you don't want reviews posted under a teammate's name.
